--- table #3  id=S3.T1.2 ---
CAPTION: Table 1. 2-bit Sign-Magnitude symmetric distance penalty assignment. A dimension contributes zero distance when signs agree and a positive penalty when signs differ; the penalty magnitude is determined by the two magnitude bits.
   | Category | Same sign | Different sign
   | Both strong | 0 0 | 4 4
   | One strong, one weak | 0 0 | 2 2
   | Both weak | 0 0 | 1 1

