--- table #17  id=S7.T14.2.1 ---
CAPTION: Table 14. Positioning of QuIVer against related systems. “BQ-native topology” indicates whether graph edge selection and pruning operate entirely in binary-quantized metric space.
   | System | Quantization role | BQ-native topology | Training
   | HNSW ( 4 ) | Storage compression or search acceleration | No | None
   | DiskANN ( 5 ) | PQ for memory-resident distance; SSD for vectors | No | PQ codebook
   | RaBitQ ( 12 ) | Distance estimator with error bounds + rotation | No | Rotation matrix
   | SVS ( 37 ) | Locally-adaptive compression for streaming search | No | Per-cluster
   | VSAG ( 33 ) | SQ/FP16 for distance acceleration in production | No | None
   | Flash ( 42 ) | Compact coding to accelerate construction distance | No | None
   | PAG ( 44 ) | Projection-based routing to reduce distance evals | No | None
   | QuIVer | Graph construction, navigation, and hot-path layout | Yes | None
